  "summary": "Recent preprints propose new alignment, peptide prioritization, and TIMS benchmarking approaches, pressing for shared evaluation standards.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is computational processing of mass spectrometry data, with each item addressing a different stage. Bromo, a transformer model, ranks peptide precursors by relative MS response with charge state for targeted experiments, outperforming sequence-based methods and allowing fine-tuning. maxiM/Ze applies OpenCV image recognition to LC-HRMS extracted ion chromatograms for automated peak alignment and reports validation. TIMS-Bench shifts to evaluation, benchmarking MZmine, MS-DIAL, and MetaboScape across ten public and three benchmark datasets while releasing ground-truth data and code. The contribution is methodological rather than a unified result, and all three items are preprints that have not undergone peer review.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-05-30"
}
